er","reason":"Performance – Flow Conditioning","type":"Performance","geometry":"Profile modification to brake duct winglets.","description":"The winglet geometry change helps improve the flow management at the back of the car and around the rear tyre.","source":"https://www.fia.com/system/files/decision-document/2026_chinese_grand_prix_-_car_presentation_submissions.pdf"}]},{"team":"Aston Martin","updates":[]},{"team":"Haas","updates":[{"component":"Rear Impact Structure","reason":"Performance - Local Load","type":"Performance","geometry":"Small winglet placed on top of the Rear Impact Structure","description":"The winglet is shaped to promote upwash, which in turn improves the local aerodynamic characteristics and results in a corresponding increase in load.","source":"https://www.fia.com/system/files/decision-document/2026_chinese_grand_prix_-_car_presentation_submissions.pdf"}]},{"team":"Audi","updates":[{"component":"Front Wing","reason":"Performance - Local Load","type":"Performance","geometry":"Updated front wing flap and end plate geometry","description":"The new flap and end plate lead to improved flow characteristics travelling further downstream along the car – locally and globally more efficient.","source":"https://www.fia.com/system/files/decision-document/2026_chinese_grand_prix_-_car_presentation_submissions.pdf"},{"component":"Nose","reason":"Performance - Local Load","type":"Performance","geometry":"Updated nose design","description":"In combination with the above mentioned step, the updated nose design allows a more efficient load extraction all along the slope.","source":"https://www.fia.com/system/files/decision-document/2026_chinese_grand_prix_-_car_presentation_submissions.pdf"}]},{"team":"Alpine","updates":[]},{"team":"Cadillac","updates":[{"component":"Diffuser","reason":"Performance - Local Load cascade","type":"Performance","geometry":"Trailing edge detail changes on diffuser winglet","description":"Modifications made to the trailing edge le